            <ArticleTitle>Building ProteomeTools based on a complete synthetic human proteome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>259-262</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/nmeth.4153</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe ProteomeTools, a project building molecular and digital tools from the human proteome to facilitate biomedical research. Here we report the generation and multimodal liquid chromatography-tandem mass spectrometry analysis of &gt;330,000 synthetic tryptic peptides representing essentially all canonical human gene products, and we exemplify the utility of these data in several applications. The resource (available at http://www.proteometools.org) will be extended to &gt;1 million peptides, and all data will be shared with the community via ProteomicsDB and ProteomeXchange.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
